<ESC>[2m<TS><ESC>[0m <ESC>[32m INFO<ESC>[0m target use invoked <ESC>[3mtarget<ESC>[0m<ESC>[2m=<ESC>[0mstaging
Error: apprafter::target::invalid_config

  × target config at <SANDBOX>/apprafter-config/targets/staging/
  │ credentials.yaml: not a valid target credentials map (line 1, column 16)
  help: <SANDBOX>/apprafter-config/targets/staging/credentials.yaml
        could not be read as target `staging`'s configuration: it was edited
        by hand or written by an incompatible CLI version. Fix it by hand (it
        is a small YAML file), or restore it from a backup. Otherwise remove
        the target with `apprafter target remove staging`, which takes a
        target it cannot read, and add it again with `apprafter target add
        staging --provider hetzner-cloud …`, its token too. The removal also
        deletes the target's local state: the record of its server, the cached
        kubeconfig and the Argo CD password. If a server is recorded, fix or
        restore the file first. After adding the target again, `apprafter
        import --target staging` rebuilds the record from the provider; the
        kubeconfig and the password are fetched again on first use.

